    {
      "id": "evt_columbia_8e1e1909",
      "name": "Use of Artificial Intelligence in Financial Risk Management",
      "type": "Academic",
      "location_id": "loc_columbia_butler",
      "community_id": "com_columbia_general",
      "description": "&lt;p&gt;With the ongoing, rapid deployment of AI in investment management, Artificial Intelligence is beginning to play a key role in the evolution of risk management. For example, large language models (LLMs) are used in security analysis, trained on customized data sets to provide a higher degree of accuracy for investment analysis than could be conducted by an individual security analyst. In operational risk, AI models are trained to classify and tag policy content against regulatory taxonomies, reducing manual review cycles and enhancing audit readiness. Of course, cybersecurity is a key focus for AI where machine learning algorithms analyze network traffic and identify cyber attacks.&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;AI and machine learning are transformative technologies that are fundamentally reshaping investment management and risk management approaches from the realm of qualitative to insightful quantitative outcomes. This panel discussion aims to provide perspectives into the evolving landscape of artificial intelligence&amp;#39;s application in financial industry risk management.&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Panelists:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Sushant Choudhary, &lt;/strong&gt;Head of Fixed Income Risk, Morgan Stanley&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Yakov Shenkman, &lt;/strong&gt;Director - Risk &amp;amp; Quantitative Analysis (RQA), BlackRock&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cindy Williams, &lt;/strong&gt;US Head of Risk Governance and Policy, Scotiabank&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Moderator:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Navin Sharma, &lt;/strong&gt;Part-Time Faculty, Enterprise Risk Management&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;Register &lt;a href=\"https://www.eventbrite.com/e/use-of-artificial-intelligence-in-financial-risk-management-registration-1537361151589?aff=oddtdtcreator\" target=\"_blank\"&gt;here&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;This is a hybrid event and will be hosted both in person and via Zoom. Registered guests will receive a Zoom link prior to the event.&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;In Person Location:&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;Butler Library, Room 203&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;535 W 114th Street, New York, NY 10027&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;For questions about this event, please contact Joshua Gleich, &lt;a href=\"mailto:jg4173@columbia.edu\" target=\"_blank\"&gt;jg4173@columbia.edu&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;To obtain additional information about program offerings at Columbia University&amp;rsquo;s School of Professional Studies, please contact an Admissions Counselor at &lt;a href=\"mailto:inquire@sps.columbia.edu\" target=\"_blank\"&gt;inquire@sps.columbia.edu&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;If you require closed captioning, sign-language interpretation, or any other disability accommodations, please contact Disability Services, &lt;a href=\"mailto:disability@columbia.edu\" target=\"_blank\"&gt;disability@columbia.edu&lt;/a&gt;, at least 10 days in advance.&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;Please visit &lt;a href=\"https://preparedness.columbia.edu/\" target=\"_blank\"&gt;Columbia University&amp;rsquo;s Hub for Emergency Preparedness&lt;/a&gt; to stay up to date on the latest campus health and safety policies.&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;This event is open to individuals irrespective of identity and sex.&lt;/p&gt;",
      "start_date": "2025-12-01T21:00:00+00:00",
      "end_date": "2025-12-01T23:00:00+00:00",
