    {
      "id": "evt_columbia_b52cf97e",
      "name": "Joy Goddess: A&rsquo;Lelia Walker and the Harlem Renaissance",
      "type": "Academic",
      "location_id": "loc_columbia_main",
      "community_id": "com_columbia_general",
      "description": "&lt;p&gt;Dubbed the &amp;ldquo;joy goddess of Harlem&amp;rsquo;s 1920s&amp;rdquo; by poet Langston Hughes, A&amp;rsquo;Lelia Walker, daughter of millionaire entrepreneur Madam C.J. Walker, and author A&amp;rsquo;Lelia Bundles&amp;rsquo;s great-grandmother and namesake, is a fascinating figure whose legendary parties and &amp;ldquo;Dark Tower&amp;rdquo; salon helped define the Harlem Renaissance. After inheriting her mother&amp;rsquo;s hair-care enterprise, A&amp;rsquo;Lelia Walker would become America&amp;rsquo;s first high-profile black heiress and a prominent patron of the arts. Joy Goddess takes readers inside her three New York homes&amp;mdash;a mansion, a townhouse, and a pied-&amp;agrave;-terre&amp;mdash;where she entertained Hughes, Zora Neale Hurston, Paul Robeson, Florence Mills, James Weldon Johnson, Carl Van Vechten, W.E.B. DuBois, and other cultural, social, and intellectual luminaries of the Roaring Twenties.&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=\"https://www.eventbrite.com/e/1680954713799?aff=oddtdtcreator\" target=\"_blank\"&gt;Register here.&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;For questions about this event, please contact George Calderaro (gc2212@columbia.edu ).&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;To obtain additional information about program offerings at Columbia University&amp;rsquo;s School of Professional Studies, please contact an Admissions Counselor at&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=\"https://www.eventbrite.com/e/joy-goddess-alelia-walker-and-the-harlem-renaissance-registration-1680954713799?aff=oddtdtcreator\" target=\"_blank\"&gt;inquire@sps.columbia.edu&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;If you require closed captioning, sign-language interpretation or any other disability accommodations, please contact Disability Services,&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=\"https://www.eventbrite.com/e/joy-goddess-alelia-walker-and-the-harlem-renaissance-registration-1680954713799?aff=oddtdtcreator\" target=\"_blank\"&gt;disability@columbia.edu&lt;/a&gt;, at least 10 days in advance.&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;Please visit&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=\"https://preparedness.columbia.edu/\" target=\"_blank\"&gt;Columbia University&amp;rsquo;s Hub for Emergency Preparedness&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;to stay up to date on the latest campus health and safety policies.&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;This event is open to individuals irrespective of identity and sex.&lt;/p&gt;",
