      "location_id": "loc_columbia_main",
      "community_id": "com_columbia_general",
      "description": "&lt;p&gt;The&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=\"https://cancerdynamics.columbia.edu\" target=\"_blank\"&gt;Herbert and Florence Irving Institute for Cancer Dynamics&lt;/a&gt; will continue its seminar series on the topic of mathematical sciences underpinning cancer research. The monthly seminars take place on the second Wednesday of the month, 2:00-3:00 PM EST. The presentations are open to the Columbia community (in person and online) and to researchers outside Columbia (via Zoom).&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;On &lt;strong&gt;Wednesday, January 14th (2:00 PM ET)&lt;/strong&gt;, IICD welcomes Dr. Matthew G. Jones from MIT. Seminar hosted by Dr. Jellert Gaublomme. The seminar will take place in person in Schermerhorn Hall 603 (Morningside Heights campus). If you wish to attend the seminar remotely, please register using the following link: &lt;a href=\"https://columbiauniversity.zoom.us/meeting/register/8BKD8L-xQZWOaZlQ6Kz6qQ\" target=\"_blank\"&gt;https://columbiauniversity.zoom.us/meeting/register/8BKD8L-xQZWOaZlQ6Kz6qQ&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Title: &lt;/strong&gt;TBA&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Abstract: &lt;/strong&gt;TBA&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bio: &lt;/strong&gt;Matthew G. Jones runs the Jones Lab at MIT. He previously was a Postdoctoral Fellow at Stanford, where he was supported by an NCI Early-Career K99/R00 Fellowship. Before that, he earned his PhD from UCSF where he was a Discovery Fellow. Originally from Pasadena, CA, he graduated from UC Berkeley with a degree in Computer Science.&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;If you would like to meet one-on-one (possibly via Zoom) or attend the lunch or dinner with the speaker, please contact the event organizer.&lt;/p&gt;",
      "start_date": "2026-01-14T19:00:00+00:00",
      "end_date": "2026-01-14T20:00:00+00:00",
      "category": [
        "EDUCATION",
        "SCIENCE",
        "TECH"
      ],
