      "id": "evt_nyu_physics_event7594",
      "name": "A Perspective on (Many-body) Localization — Facts and Work in Progress",
      "description": "The talk will present numerical investigations into the fate of Anderson localization in the presence of short-range interactions, i.e., many-body localization (MBL). The first part offers a brief overview of the field, focusing on the dynamical behavior of two key observables: entanglement entropy and sublattice imbalance. The second part highlights a concept of many-body dynamics that we introduced recently: the “potential-energy surface.” This concept provides an analogy between the relaxation of a many-body state viewed in Fock space and a previously unexplored variant of a percolation problem. Potential implications for MBL phase diagrams will also be briefly discussed.",
      "start_date": "2025-12-05T10:00:00+00:00",
