      "description": "Experience the elegance of the Classical era in this midday concert featuring Fortepiano and Strings students performing works by Mozart, Haydn, and Stamitz. Hear these masterpieces come to life on a reproduction Viennese fortepiano with 5 1/2 octaves—an instrument prized for its distinctive sound and touch, offering an authentic glimpse into the music of Mozart’s time.Program:Mozart-- Sonata for piano in D major, K. 311, Allegro con spiritoHaydn-- Sonata for piano in C major Hob:50, Allegro and Adagio Stamitz--Sonata for viola and piano in Bb major, Andante moderato Clement--Sonata for piano in Bb major, Op. 24 no. 2, Allegro con brio Mozart-- Sonata for piano in A minor, K. 310, Andante cantabileMozart--Sonata for piano in D major, K. 284, Allegro ",
