      "id": "evt_newschool_ef969119",
      "name": "Carnegie Hall Presents | The New School's New York String Orchestra 12-24",
      "type": "Performance",
      "location_id": "loc_newschool_main",
      "community_id": "com_newschool",
      "description": "A festive culmination of the celebrated New York String Orchestra Seminar (NYSOS), a national pre-professional program that has mentored outstanding emerging musicians since 1969 and boasts alumni including Yo-Yo Ma, cello; Karina Canellakis, conductor; current and former members of the Guarneri, Dover, Orion, Emerson, and Juilliard string quartets, and members in major orchestras in every state of the U.S.  Jaime Laredo, conductorAnna Polonsky, soloistALL-MOZART PROGRAMOverture to The Marriage of FigaroSymphony No. 40Piano Concerto No. 27 in B-flat Major, K. 595 Tickets $24 - $88 available at the Carnegie Hall box office.The New York String Orchestra Seminar (NYSOS) is a program of the Mannes School of Music's New School Concerts Dept. In its 57 year history, the NYSOS has never charged the students (ages 16 to 23) in the program to participate, and also covers housing, meals, and local transportation during the intensive 10-day program that incudes daily orchestral rehearsals and chamber music sessions with some of the nation's most celebrated musicians to introduce of philosophy of applying a chamber music approach to orchestral playing. To learn more about the program, its more than 2500 alumni, and how you can apply or support - visit nysos.org ",
