    {
      "id": "evt_newschool_8f30d2aa",
      "name": "Schneider Concerts Presents | Ulysses Quartet",
      "type": "Performance",
      "location_id": "loc_newschool_main",
      "community_id": "com_newschool",
      "description": "Ulysses Quartet 10 years after their New York debut on this series, the Ulysses Quartet returns as our 2025-2026 Curating/Performing ensemble. In the first of three concerts, they perform works of  Claude Debussy, Felix Mendelssohn, a world premiere of a Schneider Concerts co-commission, \"Tina Davidson's \"Just before Light\", and arrangements of folks songs from the members' heritage.Christina Bouey, violinRhiannon Banerdt, violinPeter Dudek, violaGrace Ho, celloTina Davidson: \"Just Before Light\" (2025)—World premiere of Schneider Concerts co-commissionClaude Debussy: String Quartet in G minor, Op. 10 (1893)Traditional —celebrating Ulysses Quartet members' cultural roots in Taiwan, Ireland, Poland, and the United States with folk song arrangementsFelix Mendelssohn: String Quartet in F minor, Op. 80 (1847).This concert will be approximately 1 hour and 40 minutes, including intermission 12:30p.m. pre-concert talk with Dana Kelley requires separate $5 ticket purchase - click here.This concert is available as a pay-what-you-wish simultaneous on-line broadcast for those who can't attend in person. That means register for free or choose to pay up to $20—the price of an in-person ticket. The price is entirely up to you—no pressure. We just want you to enjoy the music. Register to receive livestream link here. This concert is part of the Schneider Concerts 2025-26 season — 6 mainstage concerts featuring exceptional emerging ensembles, plus pre-concert talks, livestreams, and free short programs at community partner venues.Explore the season here. ",
