    {
      "id": "evt_newschool_b271051f",
      "name": "2026 Management and Social Justice Conference",
      "type": "Conference",
      "location_id": "loc_newschool_main",
      "community_id": "com_newschool",
      "description": "The 2026 Management and Social Justice Conference (MSJC) invites scholars, practitioners, artists, technologists, policymakers, and students to join us at Parsons School of Design, The New School, in New York City. From April 29 to May 1, 2026, we will explore how entrepreneurship can serve as a vehicle for social justice through diverse epistemologies and praxis. In this gathering, we particularly foreground domains such as poverty and economic exclusion, women’s and minority entrepreneurship, religion and spirituality in enterprise, and emerging entrepreneurial responses to homelessness, food deserts, immigration, and displacement. We also invite new, experimental, and unforeseen approaches through our Novel & Emerging Perspectives track.The conference will also result in a published conference proceedings of extended abstracts and a peer reviewed edited volume to be published Springer.Submission deadline: November 30, 2025. ",
