      "name": "Norman E. Alexander Celebration of Collections",
      "type": "Academic",
      "location_id": "loc_virtual",
      "community_id": "com_columbia_general",
      "description": "&lt;p&gt;This year&amp;#39;s annual NEA Celebration of Collections has an early modern focus, where three scholars will discuss their research on what we find in books when we look beyond the actual texts - at annotations, illustrations, and other paratexts. Professor Elisheva Carlebach (Columbia University) will discuss a colorful manuscript on the Jewish calendar; Dr. Eugene Matanky (Tel Aviv University) will share his research on a group of Kabbalists who shared their knowledge on the margins of their books; and Professor Edward Fram (Ben Gurion University) will share his research on a manuscript that highlights practical of the quintessential legal work the&amp;nbsp;&lt;em&gt;Shulhan &amp;#39;Arukh&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;at the beginning of its publication.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=\"https://columbiauniversity.zoom.us/webinar/register/WN_9OCuFVtUTTWnI-hm97Kjtw\" target=\"_blank\"&gt;Register here&lt;/a&gt;!&lt;/p&gt;",
