    {
      "id": "evt_columbia_58d8b867",
      "name": "Situational Awareness",
      "type": "Academic",
      "location_id": "loc_virtual",
      "community_id": "com_columbia_general",
      "description": "&lt;p&gt;Situational Awareness applies to all situations: being aware of where you are and to what is happening around you; being alert to potential threats to your health and safety and being cognizant of emergency exits and other paths to safety.&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;You will learn:&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;ul&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;How&amp;nbsp;situational&amp;nbsp;awareness&amp;nbsp;can keep you safe.&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;&amp;ldquo;What are the odds?&amp;rdquo;-being informed to make good decisions for your personal safety.&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;Techniques to develop&amp;nbsp;awareness.&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;Personal safety resources&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;Run. Hide. Fight. &amp;ndash; a strategy for your personal safety in emergency situations&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;/ul&gt;",
