    {
      "id": "evt_columbia_c1bc3714",
      "name": "A Festival of Nine Lessons &amp; Carols: hymns, carols, and readings",
      "type": "Performance",
      "location_id": "loc_columbia_main",
      "community_id": "com_columbia_general",
      "description": "&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Lessons &amp;amp; Carols&lt;/em&gt; is a fantastic service of readings, hymns, and carols for Christmas and Advent. Janet Yieh returns to conduct the St. Paul&amp;rsquo;s Chapel Christmas Choir, James Wetzel will play the organ, and students, faculty, and staff from across the university will read the nine lessons. Please join us for this wonderful Christmas festival.&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;PROGRAM&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;Once in Royal David&amp;rsquo;s City&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;Jesus Christ the Apple Tree&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;Adam Lay Ybounden&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;People Look East&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;In the Bleak Midwinter&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;Rise Up Shepherd and Follow&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;Gentle Mary Laid Her Child (in a new arrangement by Janet Yieh)&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;Silent Night&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;Angels We Have Heard on High&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;The Word Was God&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;O Come All Ye Faithful&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;Hark! The Herald Angels Sing&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Image: The Altar of the Three Kings (1507), on linden wood, by Hans Baldung Grien (1484&amp;ndash;1545). Now in the Gem&amp;auml;ldegalerie, Berlin.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Live at St. Paul&amp;rsquo;s Chapel &amp;mdash;&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/live/3nftOlU7Kug\" target=\"_blank\"&gt;or, watch on YouTube&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;If you don&amp;rsquo;t have a current Columbia ID, you MUST register by clicking the blue &amp;quot;register&amp;quot; button below. (Please do not use the same email address to register multiple people; this will confuse the system.)&amp;nbsp;&lt;em&gt;Registration will close at 11am sharp the day before the concert.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;",
      "start_date": "2025-12-05T23:00:00+00:00",
      "end_date": "2025-12-06T00:15:00+00:00",
      "category": [
