    {
      "id": "evt_columbia_43eaf34f",
      "name": "Tribute to Erik Barnouw: Special Panel and Screening",
      "type": "Academic",
      "location_id": "loc_columbia_main",
      "community_id": "com_columbia_general",
      "description": "&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Tribute to Erik Barnouw&amp;rsquo;s &lt;em&gt;Documentary: A History of the Non-Fiction Film&lt;/em&gt; (1974) &lt;/strong&gt;honors the founder of the School of the Arts Film Division on the occasion of the School&amp;rsquo;s 60th Anniversary. Books on media that Barnouw wrote also include &lt;em&gt;Tube of Plenty: The Evolution of American TV &lt;/em&gt;(1990). Screening highlights include Barnouw talking about US elections for Paper Tiger TV (1992), &lt;em&gt;Hiroshima/Nagasaki, August 1945&lt;/em&gt; (1970), the film edited in the Columbia Film Department from US national archives footage, and 1930s US documentary classic about the Great Depression&amp;mdash;&lt;em&gt;The Plow That Broke the Plains &lt;/em&gt;(Pare Lorentz, 1936). A panel of&amp;nbsp;film scholars will comment on Barnouw&amp;rsquo;s contribution to film and media history and documentary today.&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;Co-sponsored by Film and Media Studies at Columbia University School of the Arts and the Faculty Seminars in &amp;quot;Sites of Cinema.&amp;rdquo;&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;7 PM: Panel&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=\"https://arts.columbia.edu/profiles/joshua-glick\" target=\"_blank\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Joshua Glick&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;, Adjunct Associate Professor, Film, Columbia University; Associate Professor of Film &amp;amp; Electronic Arts at Bard College&lt;br /&gt;\n&lt;strong&gt;Dee Dee Hallek&lt;/strong&gt;, Founder, Paper Tiger TV, Professor Emerita UC-San Diego&lt;br /&gt;\n&lt;a href=\"https://arts.columbia.edu/profiles/nico-baumbach\" target=\"_blank\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nico Baumbach&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;, Associate Professor of Film and Media Studies, Columbia University&lt;br /&gt;\n&lt;strong&gt;Charles Musser&lt;/strong&gt;, Professor of Film, Yale University&lt;br /&gt;\n&lt;a href=\"https://arts.columbia.edu/profiles/jane-m-gaines\" target=\"_blank\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Jane Gaines&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;, Professor of Film and Media Studies, Columbia University&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;8:15 PM: Screening&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Erik Barnouw Looks at Television and Elections &lt;/em&gt;(Paper Tiger TV, 1992), 28 min.&lt;br /&gt;\n&lt;em&gt;The Plow That Broke the Plains &lt;/em&gt;(Pare Lorentz, US, 1936), 30 min.&lt;br /&gt;\n&lt;em&gt;Hiroshima/Nagasaki, August 1945&lt;/em&gt; (1970), 1 min. clip&lt;/p&gt;",
      "start_date": "2025-12-06T00:00:00+00:00",
      "end_date": "2025-12-06T02:15:00+00:00",
      "category": [
        "ARTS",
        "EDUCATION",
