    {
      "id": "evt_columbia_ab3825ff",
      "name": "HICCC Seminar Series - Scientific Seminar",
      "type": "Seminar",
      "location_id": "loc_columbia_main",
      "community_id": "com_columbia_general",
      "description": "&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Michel Sadelain, MD, PhD&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br /&gt;\nHerbert and Florence Irving Professor of Medicine&amp;nbsp;&lt;br /&gt;\nDepartment of Medicine, Hematology &amp;amp; Oncology&lt;br /&gt;\nProgram: Precision Oncology and Systems Biology (POSB)&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;Title:&amp;nbsp;&lt;em&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Antigen sensitivity, logic gating and persistence of CAR T cells&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Description&lt;/strong&gt;:&amp;nbsp;As a pioneer in CAR-T therapy,&amp;nbsp;Dr. Sadelain has brought revolutionary changes to cancer treatment: successfully using retroviral vectors to genetically engineer T cells; being the first to introduce the CD28 co-stimulatory domain into the CAR structure, designing the &amp;quot;second-generation&amp;quot; CAR,&amp;nbsp;establishing the feasibility of CAR-T cell therapy; being the first to prove that the CD19 molecule found on the surface of blood cells can serve as an effective target for CAR-T cells, advancing clinical trials for CAR-T cell therapy, achieving significant therapeutic effects. mammals.&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;Dr. Sadelain continues to deepen the understanding of CAR-T cell therapy, including improving the antigen sensitivity of CAR-T cells, developing new strategies to regulate CAR-T activation with logic gating, and using CRISPR technology to enhance the potency, durability, and safety of CAR-T cells. These efforts aim to surmount resistance mechanisms conferred by tumor cells and their microenvironment, thereby broadening the applicability of CAR-T cell therapy across a spectrum of cancer types.&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The event is IN-PERSON ONLY.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;",
      "start_date": "2025-12-10T21:00:00+00:00",
      "end_date": "2025-12-10T22:00:00+00:00",
      "category": [
        "HEALTH",
        "TECH",
        "EDUCATION"
      ],
      "source": "columbia",
      "source_group": "Columbia",
      "metadata": {
        "source_url": "https://events.columbia.edu/cal/event/eventView.do?b=de&calPath=%2Fpublic%2Fcals%2FMainCal&guid=CAL-00bbdb7c-983132a8-0198-32e99470-000042e1events%40columbia.edu&recurrenceId=",
        "source_name": "Columbia University",
